The error log indicates a segmentation fault during the `test_malloc` test case. The fault occurs after the zbus listener callback `s1_cb` is executed.

Upon inspection of `tests/subsys/zbus/dyn_channel/src/main.c`, two issues are identified:

1.  The listener callback `s1_cb` calls `zbus_chan_finish()`. According to the zbus documentation, this function should only be called by an observer that has previously claimed the channel. A simple listener, like `s1`, does not claim the channel and should not call `zbus_chan_finish()`. This incorrect API usage is the likely cause of the crash, as it may lead to undefined behavior within the zbus subsystem, especially when heap memory operations have occurred (as in `test_malloc`).

2.  The `test_malloc` function contains a double-free bug: `k_free(actual_message_data->reference); k_free(actual_message_data->reference);`. This will corrupt the heap and cause unpredictable behavior. While this does not appear to be the cause of the immediate crash shown in the log (which happens before this code is executed), it is a critical bug that must be fixed.

The fix involves correcting both of these issues in the test application.

